      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    int nbodies;\n    if (fread(&nbodies, sizeof(nbodies), 1, stdin) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    size_t count = (size_t)nbodies * 6;\n    float *tmp = (float *)malloc(count * sizeof(float));\n    if (!tmp) { perror(\"malloc\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n    if (fread(tmp, count * sizeof(float), 1, stdin) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n        free(tmp);\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    float * restrict px = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict py = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict pz = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict vx = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict vy = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    float * restrict vz = (float *)malloc((size_t)nbodies * sizeof(float));\n    if (!px || !py || !pz || !vx || !vy || !vz) {\n        perror(\"malloc\");\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        px[i] = tmp[6*i];\n        py[i] = tmp[6*i+1];\n        pz[i] = tmp[6*i+2];\n        vx[i] = tmp[6*i+3];\n        vy[i] = tmp[6*i+4];\n        vz[i] = tmp[6*i+5];\n    }\n    free(tmp);\n\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n        for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n            // Force computation and velocity update\n            #pragma omp for simd schedule(static)\n            for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n                float fx = 0.0f, fy = 0.0f, fz = 0.0f;\n                const float xi = px[i], yi = py[i], zi = pz[i];\n\n                int j = 0;\n                // Unroll by 4 preserving exact accumulation order\n                for (; j + 3 < nbodies; j += 4) {\n                    float dx0 = px[j]   - xi;\n                    float dy0 = py[j]   - yi;\n                    float dz0 = pz[j]   - zi;\n                    float sqrd0 = dx0*dx0 + dy0*dy0 + dz0*dz0 + SOFTENING;\n                    float inv0 = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd0);\n                    float inv3_0 = inv0 * inv0 * inv0;\n                    fx += dx0 * inv3_0;\n                    fy += dy0 * inv3_0;\n                    fz += dz0 * inv3_0;\n\n                    float dx1 = px[j+1] - xi;\n                    float dy1 = py[j+1] - yi;\n                    float dz1 = pz[j+1] - zi;\n                    float sqrd1 = dx1*dx1 + dy1*dy1 + dz1*dz1 + SOFTENING;\n                    float inv1 = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd1);\n                    float inv3_1 = inv1 * inv1 * inv1;\n                    fx += dx1 * inv3_1;\n                    fy += dy1 * inv3_1;\n                    fz += dz1 * inv3_1;\n\n                    float dx2 = px[j+2] - xi;\n                    float dy2 = py[j+2] - yi;\n                    float dz2 = pz[j+2] - zi;\n                    float sqrd2 = dx2*dx2 + dy2*dy2 + dz2*dz2 + SOFTENING;\n                    float inv2 = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd2);\n                    float inv3_2 = inv2 * inv2 * inv2;\n                    fx += dx2 * inv3_2;\n                    fy += dy2 * inv3_2;\n                    fz += dz2 * inv3_2;\n\n                    float dx3 = px[j+3] - xi;\n                    float dy3 = py[j+3] - yi;\n                    float dz3 = pz[j+3] - zi;\n                    float sqrd3 = dx3*dx3 + dy3*dy3 + dz3*dz3 + SOFTENING;\n                    float inv3_3 = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd3);\n                    float inv3_3b = inv3_3 * inv3_3 * inv3_3;\n                    fx += dx3 * inv3_3b;\n                    fy += dy3 * inv3_3b;\n                    fz += dz3 * inv3_3b;\n                }\n\n                // Tail loop for remaining bodies\n                for (; j < nbodies; ++j) {\n                    float dx = px[j] - xi;\n                    float dy = py[j] - yi;\n                    float dz = pz[j] - zi;\n                    float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n                    float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n                    float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n                    fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n                    fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n                    fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n                }\n\n                vx[i] += DT*fx;\n                vy[i] += DT*fy;\n                vz[i] += DT*fz;\n            }\n\n            // Position update (separate loop to avoid race on positions)\n            #pragma omp for simd schedule(static)\n            for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n                px[i] += vx[i]*DT;\n                py[i] += vy[i]*DT;\n                pz[i] += vz[i]*DT;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Write output in original Body layout (six floats per body)\n    float *out = (float *)malloc(count * sizeof(float));\n    if (!out) { perror(\"malloc\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        out[6*i]   = px[i];\n        out[6*i+1] = py[i];\n        out[6*i+2] = pz[i];\n        out[6*i+3] = vx[i];\n        out[6*i+4] = vy[i];\n        out[6*i+5] = vz[i];\n    }\n    if (fwrite(out, count * sizeof(float), 1, stdout) != 1) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n        free(out);\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n    free(out);\n\n    free(px); free(py); free(pz); free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Integrating SoA layout, restrict-qualified pointers, manual 4x unrolling preserving exact summation order, and a single OpenMP parallel region spanning all iterations with SIMD worksharing loops will reduce thread-creation overhead, improve cache locality, enable vectorization across bodies, and keep the force/position update barrier minimal—outperforming any individual transformation.",
  "notes": "The fused velocity+force loop is separated from position updates by an implicit barrier to avoid data races on positions. Static scheduling balances uniform per-i work. The output is reconstructed into the original Body layout for byte-exact comparison.",
